":[{"text":"இயம்பு","lemma":"இயம்பு","gloss":"sound"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"habitual relative participle"}],"gloss":"sounding"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"குன்ற","parts":[{"text":"குன்ற","lemma":"குன்ற","gloss":"of the hills"}],"gloss":"of the hills","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நாடன்","parts":[{"text":"நாடன்","lemma":"நாடன்","gloss":"lord of the land"}],"gloss":"lord of the land"},{"surface":"கண்ட","parts":[{"text":"கண்ட","lemma":"கண்ட","gloss":"that saw"}],"gloss":"that saw","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"எம்","parts":[{"text":"எம்","lemma":"யாம்","gloss":"my"}],"gloss":"my"},{"surface":"கண்ணே","parts":[{"text":"கண்","lemma":"கண்","gloss":"eye"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"eyes indeed"}]}],"literal":"Even as we bear our love, they, on their own, / because of their intimacy, wept, O friend! / The children with sparse hair who guide the calves, / seeing the blossoming stage of the common ground's Vēṅkai tree, / without climbing it, raised a protective clamor / which sounds inside the sky-touching mountain clefts / of the lord of the hilly land, whom my eyes saw.","translation":"O friend! Even as I try to bear my love, my eyes, acting on their own out of close intimacy, have wept. They are the eyes that saw the lord of the hilly land, where the sparse-haired children herding calves look at the blooming stage of the Vēṅkai tree in the common ground and, without climbing it, raise a protective shout of warning that echoes through the sky-touching mountain clefts.","modern":"தோழியே! நான் என் காமத்தைத் தாங்கிக் கொள்ள முயன்றாலும், என் கண்கள் தங்களுக்குள்ள உரிமை உணர்வினால் தாமே அழுதுவிட்டன. கன்றுகளை மேய்க்கும் மெல்லிய தலையையுடைய சிறுவர்கள், பொதுமன்றத்தில் உள்ள வேங்கை மரம் மலர்ந்திருக்கும் பருவத்தைக் கண்டு, அதன்மேல் ஏறாமலேயே எழுப்பிய காவல் கூச்சல், வானை முட்டும் மலைப்பிளவுகளில் எதிரொலிக்கும் மலைநாட்டைச் சேர்ந்த தலைவனைப் பார்த்த என் கண்கள் அல்லவா அவை!","explanation":"This poem is spoken by the heroine to her confidante in the kuriñci (mountainous) landscape. She explains that although she tries hard to conceal her deep love and pain of separation, her eyes betray her by weeping openly. The imagery of the herding children shouting at the blooming Vēṅkai tree without climbing it represents a public warning or announcement, echoing through the deep mountain clefts. This echo symbolizes how her hidden sorrow has now become public knowledge through her tears. The blooming of the Vēṅkai tree also traditionally signals the appropriate season for marriage, intensifying her longing for the lord of the hills.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,1.1],[1.1,1.7],[1.7,2.2],[2.2,3.06],[3.06,3.3],[3.44,4.0],[4.0,4.4],[4.4,5.21],[5.21,5.9],[5.9,6.3],[6.3,6.6],[6.6,7.5],[7.5,7.7],[7.7,8.3],[8.4,9.03],[9.03,9.45],[9.45,9.77],[9.77,10.08],[10.4,10.8],[10.8,11.2],[11.2,11.36],[11.36,12.1],[12.1,13.2],[13.2,13.44],[13.52,14.01],[14.01,14.3]],"female":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,1.2],[1.2,1.7],[1.7,2.2],[2.2,2.82],[2.82,3.0],[3.13,3.8],[3.8,4.2],[4.2,5.07],[5.07,5.65],[5.65,6.38],[6.38,6.96],[6.96,7.4],[7.4,7.7],[7.7,8.2],[8.2,8.8],[8.8,9.08],[9.08,9.5],[9.5,9.92],[9.92,10.34],[10.34,10.9],[10.9,11.6],[11.6,12.8],[12.8,13.7],[13.7,14.4],[14.4,14.7],[14.7,15.0]]},"sync":[[["யாம்","we"],["எம்","our"]],[["காமம்","love"]],[["தாங்கவும்","even as we bear"]],[["தாம்","they"],["தம்","their"]],[["கெழுதகைமையின்","because of intimacy"]],[["கெழுதகைமையின்","because of intimacy"]],[["கெழுதகைமையின்","because of intimacy"],["அழுதன","wept"]],[["தோழி","O friend"]],[["கன்று","calves"],["ஆற்றுப்படுத்த","who guided"]],[["ஆற்றுப்படுத்த","who guided"]],[["புன்","sparse"],["தலைச்","headed"]],[["சிறாஅர்","children"]],[["மன்ற","of the common ground"]],[["வேங்கை","kino tree"]],[["மலர்","blossoming"],["பதம்","stage"]],[["நோக்கி","seeing"]],[["ஏறாது","without climbing"]],[["ஏறாது","without climbing"],["இட்ட","made"]],[["ஏமப்","protective"]],[["பூசல்","clamor"]],[["விண்","sky"],["தோய்","touching"]],[["விடர்","mountain cleft"],["அகத்து","inside"]],[["அகத்து","inside"],["இயம்பும்","sounding"]],[["குன்ற","of the hills"]],[["நாடன்","lord of the land"]],[["கண்ட","that saw"],["எம்","my"]],[["கண்ணே","eyes indeed"]]]}